## Agent mode: tool call visibility

When `--allowedTools ""` is lifted (Plexi IQ Stage 1), stream-json emits
`tool_use` events that are currently swallowed as `StreamEvent::Unknown`.
Wire parsing to emit in-progress tool call lines into the terminal (e.g.
`[tool: bash] ls -la`, `[tool: read] src/main.rs`) so the user can see what
the agent is doing mid-response. Already have all the JSON parsing scaffolding
in `parse_stream_event`.

## Agent mode: streaming scroll behavior polish

Tokens write into egui_term's PTY buffer; scroll position is maintained
independently. If user scrolls up mid-response, new tokens still arrive but
the view stays. Needs UX testing at scroll boundary edge cases — does the
terminal snap back on turn complete? Does it lose position mid-stream? Likely
a small fix in how write_agent_bytes interacts with the terminal's autoscroll
flag.

## Plexi IQ Native — replace claude CLI subprocess with direct Anthropic API

Current agent mode uses `claude -p` subprocess. Long-term: Plexi IQ native
mode calls the Anthropic API directly (no subprocess, full control over model,
tools, context window, cost). Secrets CLI (v2.0 P.6) is the prerequisite —
user sets ANTHROPIC_KEY via `plexi secret set`. Native mode becomes the default
once Plexi IQ Stage 1 ships (Month 3). The `claude -p` path stays as a fallback
for users without a direct API key.

## Agent mode: re-enable tool use with permission model

Currently `--allowedTools ""` forces conversational-only mode. Terminal
assistant is much more useful with bash/read/write access. Needs: (1) TTY or
non-interactive permission model so claude CLI doesn't hang waiting for a
prompt, (2) UI for surfacing pending permission requests to the user, (3)
scoping to pane's CWD. Prerequisite for Plexi IQ Stage 1 native mode.
